  "limits": [
    "No new inode/store format. Existing World, revision, and retained orphan chunk maps are the source of truth.",
    "Native sparse seek requires SDK 27+ build, macOS 27 and the updated daemon/module together. SDK 26 omits the new protocol and retains conservative kernel fallback. No macOS 26 native sparse seek qualification.",
    "Any stored chunk reports data for a full 64 KiB interval, clipped to EOF, even beyond trimmed payload length; inline files conservatively report all bytes as data. APFS can report different valid boundaries.",
    "Current CoW views query metadata keys in bounded pages without reading payloads or iterating over hole bytes. Historical flat/sorted-run views materialize metadata key lists and lack the CoW traversal bound. Dense-data hole search is proportional to contiguous chunk keys.",
    "No preallocation, hole punch or physical device extent mapping. Native acceptance uses an owned disposable private single-user mount on macOS 27.2.1 arm64; no full POSIX/APFS, power-loss or multi-user guarantee."
  ]
